/*Q21.
Write a Java program that prompts the user to enter a single letter from the alphabet series and displays the preceding letter in the alphabet series.

Input format:
  - The input is a single letter from the alphabet series.

Output format:
  - The output is the preceding letter to the user-given letter.

Note:
  - Input character must be between letters B to Z or b to z.
  - A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Subtract 1 and cast back to char. Input is guaranteed B to Z or b to z.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        char ch = sc.next().charAt(0);
        System.out.println((char) (ch - 1));
        sc.close();
    }
}
